[thin] The compliant TPU flange tapers to its circumference to mate the approved 45° countersink while its annular end is flush with the lid. These readings are at that required mating taper. Derek explicitly requested countersunk faces on both sides; insertion feel and edge durability remain untested.
alternatives: A vertical edge land requires a stepped mating pocket or a changed flare profile; a proud flange consumes the casing clearance and violates the requested flush face. The matching 45° PETG/TPU profile is the approved design.
